.TH "GLESHA-IMPORT" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-import \- register an existing full archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha import SET (\-\-file FILE | \-\-from REMOTE \-\-key KEY) [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register an existing full archive.
.PP
Registers an existing full archive. Associating an uploaded archive does not upload it again. Use configure \-\-root to bind local sources afterward.
.PP
With \-\-from or \-\-to, only their combined bucket selection may be accessed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-file FILE
Local archive.
.TP
.B \-\-key KEY
Exact remote object key.
.TP
.B \-\-root NAME=PATH
Archive root NAME=source PATH.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline ID|new
Explicit snapshot baseline.
.TP
.B \-\-date RFC3339
Known backup date in RFC3339.
.TP
.B \-\-deep\-verify
Download associated remote bytes and verify them.
.SS Buckets
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Archive source remotes, in fallback order.
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Additional buckets this command may access.
.SS Passphrases
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE|\-
Catalog passphrase file; '\-' reads stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE|\-
Archive passphrase file; '\-' reads stdin.
.SS Cloud retrieval
.TP
.B \-\-request\-retrieval
Allow retrieval charges for cold cloud objects.
.TP
.B \-\-retrieval TIER
Bulk, standard or expedited (default: bulk).
.TP
.B \-\-days N
Readable\-copy availability days (default 3; pending requests keep saved duration).
.SS Performance
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory budget, e.g. 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Maximum parallel transfers; memory may lower this limit.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Maximum parallel file hashing workers.
.SS Global options
.TP
.B \-\-format FORMAT
Result format: plain or json; status also supports table and csv (default: plain).
.TP
.B \-\-progress MODE
Progress on stderr: auto, plain, or off (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
TOML settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir DIR
Local state directory; overrides catalog.directory.
.TP
.B \-\-env FILE
Load credentials; existing process variables take priority.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
Color mode: auto, yes, or no (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-log\-level LEVEL
Diagnostic verbosity: debug, info, warn, error, or silent (default: info).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show this command's help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version and build revision.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha import old\-docs \-\-file old\-backup.tar.gz.gpg
glesha import old\-docs \-\-from b2 \-\-key backups/old\-backup.gpg
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Results and tables go to stdout. Activity, prompts, warnings, and errors go to stderr.
Use \-\-format=json for version 2 result records, one per line.
JSON diagnostics and progress use separate version 1 records on stderr; neither stream contains ANSI controls.
Use \-\-progress=off to disable progress. In plain output, redirected stderr or TERM=dumb uses step lines.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1)
